<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72433" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶμος</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷμος</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			S.
			<u>Ichn.</u>
			168
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Call.
			<u>Aet.Oxy.</u>
			2079.27
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Parth.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			31
		</span></i>, <u>Epigr.Gr.</u> (v. infr.), Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.546
		</span></i>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φροίμιον</span>), ὁ, also ἡ (v. infr.),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>way, road, path,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				290
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.248
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευρὸν οἶ. αἰθέρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					396
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁπλῆ οἶ. εἰς Ἅιδου φέρει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					239
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθὴν παρ᾽ οἶ., ἣ ᾽πὶ Λάρισαν
					φέρει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					835
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τὴν παραπλησίην οἶ. ἐμπίπτουσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Decent.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν αὐτὸν οἶ. πορευόμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					420b
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλην οἶ. ἐκπορεύεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					681
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυγρήν θ᾽ οἷ. ἔβην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					227
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Teos</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>stripe,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶμοι κυάνοιο</span>
			<i>stripes</i> or <i>layers</i> of cyanos, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.24
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>strip of land, tract, country,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκύθην ἐς οἶ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶμος ἀοιδῆς</span>
			<i>the course</i> or <i>strain</i> of song, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				451
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπέων οἶμον λιγύν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					9.47
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				2.96
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Jov.</u>
				78
			</span></i>.</div>
